CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ conversion op to vector resolves: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
The bounded reproducer sums a 3-element static range through a
ranges-style `template <class C> operator C()`, requiring
[over.match.copy] two-step copy-initialization and the
[over.best.ics]/4 exclusion of user-defined conversions for
constructor-candidate parameters.  Runtime-verified with g++ 13 and
clang++ (both compile silently and the trap-prelude binary exits 0).
